hi I'm Evan Carmichael I'm excited today  because I've been asked to speak at the  strategic sales and marketing Expo  that's happening on April 25th in York  Region which is just north of the city  here in toronto and i'm excited because  all the proceeds from this event go to  support the Alzheimer's Society of york  region and my grandfather passed away  not too long ago from Alzheimer's so  it's a cause that's very near and dear  to my heart what I'm going to be talking  about is 14 ways to turn your business  into a marketing machine and I know a  lot of entrepreneurs struggle with  promoting themselves you may have a  great product or service you may be  really good at what you do but you have  a hard time getting the word out getting  customers in getting partnerships  created and so I'm going to talk about  14 different ways you can turn your  business into that almost automated  marketing machine to have customers  coming to you some of my friends are  gonna be on the panel as well there's  gonna be Donna Messer who is Canada's  networking Queen if you want to learn  anything about networking and how to get  in front of the right people you've  gotta listen to Donna and Gary shouldice  is another friend of mine who's going to  be talking about online marketing and  how it's more than just SEO which is  what a lot of people just think about  how to basically get your word out about  your business online it seemed a great  event it's an all day event I think it's  8 a.m. in the morning to four o'clock in  the afternoon I'm going to be speaking  later on in the day but I hope your go  in and sign up and join there's going to  be some free bonuses that are given out  and some auction items including the  ability to meet with me one-on-one talk  about your business hopefully get some  good advice to help you grow for more  information there's a website let me  pull that up here it is strategic sales  and marketing dot CA and again it's  April 25th hold the event I hope you go  check it out strategic sales and  marketing dot CA and I'll see you there  you
 

